# Start here — {{KB_NAME}}

> Auto-generated at the end of deployment. Read this once.

## How to talk to the AI

Whenever you open a **new chat** with an AI agent (Claude, GPT, Cursor, Codex, etc.) and want it to work with this knowledge base, **start with this exact line**:

```
Read AGENTS.md and use it as the primary instruction for everything that follows.
```

(or in Russian:)

```
Прочитай AGENTS.md и используй его как основную инструкцию для всего, что следует дальше.
```

If you skip this step the agent has no idea this knowledge base exists, will ignore your custom voice and rules, and the special commands below will not work.

## Commands you can use in chat

After the agent has read `AGENTS.md`, these commands work:

| Command | What it does | Cost |
|---------|--------------|------|
| `!save` | Save a session summary now (decisions, conclusions, processed materials) | ~2K tokens |
| `!reflect` | Synthesize higher-level insights from accumulated facts | ~15K tokens |
| `!audit` | Full AI review of the base — contradictions, gaps, merge candidates | ~50–100K tokens |
| `!review` | Process the `review/` queue: pick up files routed for AI judgment, extract knowledge, ask for input where needed | ~5–30K tokens |
| `!populate` | Re-generate `DATA_PLACEMENT_EXAMPLES.md` (when you've changed your role YAML) | ~50 tokens |
| `!super` | Toggle operating mode: default ↔ super | 0 tokens |
| `!super on` / `!super off` | Force a mode | 0 tokens |
| `!super status` | Show current mode | 0 tokens |

## How to run the watcher

The watcher auto-processes any file you drop into `raw/<sub>/unsorted/`.

### macOS
- **Start:** double-click `watcher-start.command` (in this folder)
- **Stop:** press Ctrl+C in the terminal window that opened

### Linux
- **Start:** `./watcher.sh` from a terminal
- **Or background:** `./watcher.sh --daemon` then `./watcher.sh --stop` to stop

### Windows
- **Start:** double-click `watcher-start.bat`
- **Stop:** close the cmd window or Ctrl+C

## Manual reindex

If you didn't run the watcher and want to process accumulated raw files now:

- **macOS:** double-click `reindex.command`
- **Linux:** `./reindex.sh`
- **Windows:** double-click `reindex.bat`

